-- title:
--   Adic frame rings are complete valuation rings with fraction field C
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring with an algebra map to a field $K_0$, let $\pi \in \mathcal O$, and let $C$ be an algebraically closed field carrying a valuation $\mathrm{Valued.v}$ with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$, equipped with a $K_0$-algebra structure. Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a $C$-subalgebra source, with the $\mathcal O$-algebra structures on $R$, $K_0$ and $C$ compatible as scalar towers. Let $\varpi$ be a pseudo-uniformiser for $K_0$ in $C$, that is, an element $\varpi.\varpi \in K_0$ whose image in $C$ has valuation strictly between $0$ and $1$ and such that for every nonzero $a \in K_0$ there is $N$ with $v(\varpi)^N \le v(a) \le v(\varpi)^{-N}$. Assume `IsAdicFrame π ϖ R`: $\pi$ is irreducible, $\mathrm{algebraMap}\, R\, C$ is injective with image exactly $\{c \in C : v(c) \le 1\}$, $R$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, the elements of $K_0$ of valuation $\le 1$ in $C$ are exactly those coming from $\mathcal O$, the image of $K_0$ in $C$ is closed, and $\pi$ and $\varpi.\varpi$ have the same image in $C$. Then $R$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ in $R$, and, for the domain structure on $R$, $R$ is a valuation ring, $C$ is a fraction field of $R$, and $\mathrm{Frac}(R)$ is algebraically closed.
--
--   This identifies the ring of an adic frame for the formal upper half plane with the valuation ring $\mathcal O_C = \{v \le 1\}$ of the algebraically closed valued field $C$, a complete discretely-parametrised base over which the Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation is computed. It supports the construction of the descended quotient map on adic fibres.
